<span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Rentals</span>
<h1>50cc Motorbike Hanoi: Students Rainy Weather</h1>
<p>Student schedules do not care about the weather. Class starts at eight whether the sky is clear or the street outside is a river, and a rented 50cc that carried you happily all week becomes a different machine the moment the rain starts. The honest student position on rain is not avoidance, because avoiding it would mean avoiding your degree; it is preparation and judgment: know what the rain does to visibility, braking and route choice on a small bike, know what gear fits a student budget, and know when the correct answer is to park the bike and take the hit to the schedule. The rental counter at 112 Nguyen Van Cu, Long Bien, Hanoi, open daily from 09:00 to 21:00, rents 50cc scooters and motorbikes at 200,000 VND per day.</p>
<p>This guide belongs to the <a href="/hanoi-50cc-motorbike-rental/">50cc motorbike rental</a> hub, pairs with the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental-cost/">rental cost breakdown</a>, and complements the answers in the <a href="/faq/">FAQ</a>. The general rules live in the <a href="/motorbike-guides/riding-a-motorbike-in-hanoi-rainy-season/">rainy season riding guide</a>; this page keeps them specific to a student on a small bike with a timetable.</p>
